module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Triangulated.Opposite.Pretriangulated
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.SmallEtaleDerivedSheafHomComparisonMap
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.DerivedPushforward.MixedInternalHomPullbackIso

/-!
# Stacks 08JP, case (2): the canonical map is an isomorphism on the subcategory generated by `𝒪_S`

Let `S` be a scheme and `ε : (S_étale, 𝒪) ⟶ (S_Zar, 𝒪_S)` the morphism of ringed sites of
Stacks 08H7. `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison` is
the canonical map of Stacks 08JP,

`ε^* R𝓗om_{𝒪_S}(E, F) ⟶ R𝓗om_𝒪(ε^* E, ε^* F)`,

conditionally on the three mixed-universe data `T₂`, `e₂`, `m` of
`StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.DerivedPushforward.MixedInternalHomPullbackMap`. This
file proves it is an **isomorphism** for `E` in the strictly full saturated triangulated
subcategory of `D(𝒪_S)` generated by the structure sheaf — the hypothesis of case (2) of
Stacks 08JP, read globally.

## The proof, and where 08JP's hypothesis on `E` enters

The argument is the dévissage of Stacks 08JP, assembled abstractly in
`StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.DerivedPushforward.MixedInternalHomPullbackIso`:

* at `E = 𝒪_S` the two sides are `ε^* F` and the map is an isomorphism
  (`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback.MixedTranspose.isIso_homComparison_unit`). This
  is *proved*, from the right unitors of the two derived tensor products, the naturality of the
  two tensor–internal-Hom bijections in their first variable, and the unitality of the
  monoidality comparison of `ε^*`;
* the objects at which a shift-compatible natural transformation between triangulated functors is
  invertible form a thick triangulated subcategory, so invertibility spreads from `𝒪_S` to
  everything `𝒪_S` generates
  (`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback.MixedTranspose.isIso_app_of_generator`).

The hypothesis on `E` is the only route from the first bullet to the conclusion, and it is
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.zariskiUnitObj`-generation: `E` lies in every property of the
objects of `D(𝒪_S)ᵒᵖ` closed under isomorphisms and retracts, triangulated, and holding at the
structure sheaf. That is the global form of perfection: over a ring the perfect objects are
exactly the strictly full saturated triangulated subcategory generated by the ring
(Stacks 0ATI), on an affine scheme perfection is read over the ring (Stacks 08EB), and a perfect
complex is only *locally* a finite complex of finite free modules (Stacks 06Z0). **The two steps
of 08JP's proof that bridge the difference — that being an isomorphism is local, and that a
perfect complex is locally strictly perfect — are not formalized here**, and neither is the
identification of this generation condition with any of the `IsPerfect` predicates of this
repository. What is proved is the rest of the argument: the unit case and the dévissage out of
it.

## What remains hypothetical

Besides the three mixed-universe data `T₂`, `e₂`, `m`, which are hypotheses already in
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison`:

* `r₁`, `r₂`: the right unitors `K ⊗^L_{𝒪_S} 𝒪_S ≅ K` and `A ⊗_{T₂} ε^*𝒪_S ≅ A` of the two
  derived tensor products, with their naturality. The first is Stacks 06YU's unit; no unitor for
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.canonicalDerivedTensorProduct` exists in this development.
* `hn₁`: the naturality of the tensor–internal-Hom bijection of Stacks 08DI in its first
  variable. The fact itself is no longer a gap of this development: it is the source clause of
  Stacks 08J8, `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCurryHomEquiv_naturality_source`, and at a
  ringed space it is
  `Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomEvaluation.tensorEquivIsEvaluation`. It is still carried
  here, in the shape `MixedTranspose.TensorHomEquivNatural` asks for, which is not the shape
  either of those is stated in.
* `hn₂`, `hm`: the same naturality for the mixed bijection `e₂`, and the unitality of `m`.
* `η`: that the comparison, as a function of `E`, is the component of a shift-compatible natural
  transformation between triangulated functors.

None of these asserts that any instance of the comparison is invertible. The only invertibility
used is at `E = 𝒪_S`, and that is proved.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.zariskiUnitObj`: the structure sheaf `𝒪_S` as an object of
  `D(𝒪_S)`, placed in degree zero.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isIso_derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonAtStandardModel`: the
  comparison at the standard model is an isomorphism at every `E` generated by `𝒪_S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isIso_derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison`:
  **Stacks 08JP, case (2)**: the canonical map between the two sides is an isomorphism
  there.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08JP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08JP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08I3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08I3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08JF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08JF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08DI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08DI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06Z0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06Z0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08EB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08EB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ATI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ATI)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
  Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback
open scoped CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale

attribute [local instance 2000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

-- The source-side derived tensor product `internalHomTensorUncurried` is stated on
-- `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSpace.KFlatDerivedPullback.Modules S.toRingedSpace`, i.e. at the
-- `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf S.toRingedSpace.sheaf` spelling of the structure sheaf,
-- while the instances carrying `Category (DerivedCategory _)` on it are keyed at the
-- `structureSheafRing` spelling. The two are the same sheaf of rings by `rfl`, but
-- `structureSheafRing` is semireducible and so is not unfolded when the goal is keyed into the
-- instance discrimination tree; reaching the common normal form from the `Tensor.ringSheaf`
-- side instead needs these two Mathlib defs unfolded, which is what this does. This is the
-- same opt-in that
-- `StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.DerivedPushforward.InternalHomPullbackMap`, where
-- these functors are built, carries for the same reason.
attribute [local instance_reducible] CategoryTheory.sheafCompose
  AlgebraicGeometry.SheafedSpace.sheaf

variable (B : BigEtaleSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  [PreservesFiniteLimits (associatedModuleOfSheaf B S hS)]

/-- **The structure sheaf `𝒪_S` as an object of `D(𝒪_S)`**, placed in degree zero: the free sheaf
of modules of rank one on the Zariski site of `S`. It is the generator whose thick triangulated
closure case (2) of Stacks 08JP is about. -/
def zariskiUnitObj : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf) :=
  (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf) 0).obj
    (SheafOfModules.unit S.ringCatSheaf)

section Comparison

variable
  (T₂ : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u + 1}
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS).O)) ×
        DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u}
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS).O)) ⥤
      DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u + 1}
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS).O)))
  (e₂ : ∀ (A : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u + 1}
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS).O)))
      (K L : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u}
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS).O))),
      (A ⟶ ((derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS).obj (op K)).obj L) ≃
        (T₂.obj (A, K) ⟶ (derivedModuleULift B S hS).obj L))
  (m : internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace ⋙
        derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS ⋙ derivedModuleULift B S hS ≅
      ((derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS ⋙
          derivedModuleULift B S hS).prod
        (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)) ⋙ T₂)

variable
  (r₁ : ∀ Z : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf),
      (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace).obj (Z, zariskiUnitObj S) ≅ Z)
  (r₂ : ∀ Z : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u + 1}
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS).O)),
      T₂.obj (Z, (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS).obj
        (zariskiUnitObj S)) ≅ Z)

/-- **The comparison at the standard model is an isomorphism at every `E` generated by `𝒪_S`.**

This is
`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedInternalHomPullback.MixedTranspose.isIso_homComparison_of_generatedByOp`
at `ε`: the unit case is the computation `ε^* R𝓗om(𝒪_S, F) = ε^* F = R𝓗om(ε^*𝒪_S, ε^* F)`, and the
dévissage carries it to the thick triangulated closure of `𝒪_S`. -/
theorem isIso_derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonAtStandardModel
    (hn₁ : MixedTranspose.TensorHomEquivNatural (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf)
      (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) (tensorHomEquiv S.toRingedSpace))
    (hr₁ : MixedTranspose.RightUnitorNatural (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace)
      (zariskiUnitObj S) r₁)
    (hn₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedTensorHomEquivNatural (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) T₂ e₂)
    (hr₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedRightUnitorNatural
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) T₂ (zariskiUnitObj S) r₂)
    (hm : MixedTranspose.MonoidalityUnital
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) T₂ m (zariskiUnitObj S) r₁ r₂)
    (F : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf))
    [(MixedTranspose.comparisonSourceFunctor
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf) F).CommShift ℤ]
    [(MixedTranspose.comparisonTargetFunctor
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) F).CommShift ℤ]
    [(MixedTranspose.comparisonSourceFunctor
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf) F).IsTriangulated]
    [(MixedTranspose.comparisonTargetFunctor
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) F).IsTriangulated]
    (η : MixedTranspose.comparisonSourceFunctor
        (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf) F ⟶
      MixedTranspose.comparisonTargetFunctor
        (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)
        (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) F)
    [NatTrans.CommShift η ℤ]
    (hη : ∀ Z : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf),
      η.app (op Z) = derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonAtStandardModel B S hS T₂ e₂ m Z F)
    (E : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf))
    (hE : MixedTranspose.GeneratedByOp (zariskiUnitObj S) E) :
    IsIso (derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonAtStandardModel B S hS T₂ e₂ m E F) :=
  MixedTranspose.isIso_homComparison_of_generatedByOp
    (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf) (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS)
    (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) T₂ (tensorHomEquiv S.toRingedSpace) e₂ m
    (zariskiUnitObj S) r₁ r₂ hn₁ hr₁ hn₂ hr₂ hm F η hη E hE

/-- **Stacks 08JP, case (2), over the mixed-universe data `T₂`, `e₂`, `m`.**

The canonical map

`ε^* R𝓗om_{𝒪_S}(E, F) ⟶ R𝓗om_𝒪(ε^* E, ε^* F)`

of `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison`, between the
two sides `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.raisedDerivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHom` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.derivedSheafHomOfAssociatedModule`, is an **isomorphism** whenever
`E` lies in the strictly full saturated triangulated subcategory of `D(𝒪_S)` generated by the
structure sheaf, and `F` is arbitrary — which is the shape of case (2) of Stacks 08JP, whose
hypothesis on `E` is perfection and whose `F` is unrestricted.

The condition on `E` is what takes the statement off `E = 𝒪_S`; the conditions on the data are
listed in the module docstring. The two model identifications are isomorphisms, so the conclusion
for the canonical map is the conclusion for the comparison at the standard model. -/
@[stacks 08JP "case (2), E in the thick closure of 𝒪_S, over the data T₂, e₂, m"]
theorem isIso_derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison
    (hn₁ : MixedTranspose.TensorHomEquivNatural (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf)
      (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) (tensorHomEquiv S.toRingedSpace))
    (hr₁ : MixedTranspose.RightUnitorNatural (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace)
      (zariskiUnitObj S) r₁)
    (hn₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedTensorHomEquivNatural (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) T₂ e₂)
    (hr₂ : MixedTranspose.MixedRightUnitorNatural
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) T₂ (zariskiUnitObj S) r₂)
    (hm : MixedTranspose.MonoidalityUnital
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (internalHomTensorUncurried S.toRingedSpace) T₂ m (zariskiUnitObj S) r₁ r₂)
    (F : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf))
    [(MixedTranspose.comparisonSourceFunctor
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf) F).CommShift ℤ]
    [(MixedTranspose.comparisonTargetFunctor
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) F).CommShift ℤ]
    [(MixedTranspose.comparisonSourceFunctor
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf) F).IsTriangulated]
    [(MixedTranspose.comparisonTargetFunctor
      (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)
      (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) F).IsTriangulated]
    (η : MixedTranspose.comparisonSourceFunctor
        (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS) (derivedModuleULift B S hS)
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf) F ⟶
      MixedTranspose.comparisonTargetFunctor
        (derivedAssociatedModuleFunctorStandardModel B S hS)
        (derivedSheafHomBifunctor B S hS) F)
    [NatTrans.CommShift η ℤ]
    (hη : ∀ Z : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf),
      η.app (op Z) = derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonAtStandardModel B S hS T₂ e₂ m Z F)
    (E : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} S.ringCatSheaf))
    (hE : MixedTranspose.GeneratedByOp (zariskiUnitObj S) E) :
    IsIso (derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison B S hS T₂ e₂ m E F) := by
  have h : IsIso (derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonAtStandardModel B S hS T₂ e₂ m E F) :=
    isIso_derivedSheafHomPullbackComparisonAtStandardModel B S hS T₂ e₂ m r₁ r₂
      hn₁ hr₁ hn₂ hr₂ hm F η hη E hE
  have hinv : IsIso ((derivedModuleULift B S hS).map
      (derivedAssociatedModuleObjModelIso B S hS
        (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf).obj (op E)).obj F)).inv) :=
    Iso.isIso_inv ((derivedModuleULift B S hS).mapIso
      (derivedAssociatedModuleObjModelIso B S hS
        (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedSheafHom S.sheaf).obj (op E)).obj F)))
  rw [derivedAssociatedModuleDerivedSheafHomComparison_eq]
  exact IsIso.comp_isIso' hinv
    (IsIso.comp_isIso' h (Iso.isIso_hom (derivedSheafHomOfAssociatedModuleModelIso B S hS E F)))

end Comparison

end AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale

end
